<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 03-FEB.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 03-FEB.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Pancho-Helinda, with 120 mph winds, is in the southern Indian Ocean near 17s/85e, moving south at 9 mph. Pancho-Helinda will slowly begin to weaken this period. This storm is a major threat to shipping, but does not threaten land at this time.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.</p>
